            "date": "2026-11-18T20:00:50Z"
          },
          "message": "build: prepare releases for pre-release tags and drop go install (#118)\n\nThe module stays at `gitea.dev/cli` for 2.x, as gitea/runner does, so `go install gitea.dev/cli/cmd/gt@latest` keeps resolving to 1.x. gt therefore no longer advertises go install: the README drops it, and go-install builds point to the release installers. The extension release workflow that `gt extension create` generates installs the released gt with the install script instead of `go run …@latest`.\n\nTags such as `v2.0.0-rc1` are now published as pre-releases and no longer move the Docker `latest` tag. Version comparison follows semver pre-release ordering, so a 2.0.0-rc1 build sees 2.0.0 as newer; a Gitea release candidate still counts as its release when gating commands.\n\n`.claude/` is ignored in Git and Docker builds.\n\nReviewed-on: https://gitea.com/gitea/cli/pulls/118\n",
          "tree": {
            "url": "https://gitea.com/api/v1/repos/gitea/cli/git/trees/8e5f0e76efb402e5558271c3771e7c045e72aff055fe1d15d138f4acdcddd51a",
