        "commit": {
          "url": "https://gitea.com/api/v1/repos/gitea/cli/git/commits/5f51226031e3b86a5bc06c4efea8eaaaaf995366492bc2e3c7908b3ccf20bbe7",
          "author": {
            "name": "bircni",
            "email": "redacted@example.invalid",
            "date": "2026-11-18T19:59:08Z"
          },
          "committer": {
            "name": "bircni",
            "email": "redacted@example.invalid",
            "date": "2026-11-18T19:59:08Z"
          },
          "message": "enhance!: require --json fields and print null for absent values (#127)\n\n**Breaking:** `--json` and `--csv` now require a field list, and absent values in JSON output are `null` instead of `\"\"` or a missing key.\n\nLike gh, `--json` without fields fails with a usage error that lists the available fields. gt no longer guesses whether the word after `--json` is a field list or an argument, so adding a field can no longer change how an existing command line is parsed. `--jq` and `--template` still read every field the command declares.\n\nEvery declared field is now always present: a field without a value is `null` and an empty list is `[]`. Timestamps are RFC 3339 in UTC to the second. `gt schema` marks date-time strings, and a test checks that no output type leaves a field out.\n\nReviewed-on: https://gitea.com/gitea/cli/pulls/127\n",
          "tree": {
            "url": "https://gitea.com/api/v1/repos/gitea/cli/git/trees/6c7979c9d0d3e0c0930be5b2d8c0703396256cc07cffdca434cc5f18980584e6",
